Chapter: GaCoreTest
  cites AI chapter GeneticAlgorithm

 Runs a real genetic algorithm end to end on the generic core and requires it
 to solve the problem. Score, rank, keep the elite, cross over, mutate,
 re-run, for enough generations to actually converge.

 The problem is OneMax: a binary genome, fitness is the number of ones, and
 the optimum is the gene count exactly. It is the canonical GA benchmark, and
 it is also the shape a doctrine genome has -- one bit per lesson, include or
 exclude -- so this test doubles as the worked example for that use.

 The population is driven through ga-elitist-step directly with operators
 supplied here, rather than through ga-evolve-elitist. That is deliberate and
 it is the point of the lift: ga-evolve-elitist is bound to ga-config-default
 and therefore to a 0..1000 gene range, which would reroll a binary gene to
 three digits and destroy the genome. A domain that needs its own config
 binds it in a named wrapper, which is what gct-mutate is, and the generic
 core never has to know.

 Everything is deterministic. ga-rand-range is a pure hash of seed and index,
 so there is no real randomness and the whole run is reproducible.

 What is asserted, in order of what would survive a rewrite:

   solved          the GA reaches the known optimum. This is the product
                   working, not the plumbing being connected.
   rank descends   ranking states its own property directly.
   monotonic       elitism retains the fittest, so best fitness can never
                   fall. A ranking that stops ranking retains an arbitrary
                   prefix and this goes False.

Section: Problem

  gct-genes : Integer
  gct-genes = 24

  gct-pop-size : Integer
  gct-pop-size = 30

  gct-elite : Integer
  gct-elite = 6

  gct-gens : Integer
  gct-gens = 40

  gct-cfg : GaConfig
  gct-cfg = GaConfig { mutation-rate = 40, crossover-rate = 800, tournament-size = 3, gene-min = 0, gene-max = 1 }

 The same config with mutation switched off. The run is done twice, once with
 each, and the contrast is asserted. Crossover only recombines material that
 is already in the pool, and elitism drains the pool, so a crossover-only run
 converges on a suboptimum and stops there. Mutation is what introduces bits
 nobody had. Measured here rather than assumed: 24 of 24 with mutation, 18 of
 24 without.

  gct-cfg-nomut : GaConfig
  gct-cfg-nomut = GaConfig { mutation-rate = 0, crossover-rate = 800, tournament-size = 3, gene-min = 0, gene-max = 1 }

 Two configs differing ONLY in crossover-rate, with mutation off in both so
 crossover is the sole variable. `ga-evolve` (tournament selection, full
 replacement) runs under each and the two best-fitness sequences must DIFFER.

 That assertion is the point. crossover-rate was declared, defaulted to 800,
 and read by nothing: crossover was applied unconditionally whatever the
 config said. A knob wired to nothing produces identical output at 0 and at
 1000, so requiring a difference is what tells a connected knob from a
 decorative one, and it is the only assertion here that could have caught the
 original defect. It also gives ga-evolve and ga-tournament-select their only
 coverage in this file.

  gct-cfg-nox : GaConfig
  gct-cfg-nox = GaConfig { mutation-rate = 0, crossover-rate = 0, tournament-size = 3, gene-min = 0, gene-max = 1 }

  gct-cfg-allx : GaConfig
  gct-cfg-allx = GaConfig { mutation-rate = 0, crossover-rate = 1000, tournament-size = 3, gene-min = 0, gene-max = 1 }

 Fitness is the count of ones, so the optimum is gct-genes.

  gct-ones : GaChromosome -> Integer
  gct-ones (c) = gct-ones-loop (c.genes) 0 (c.gene-count) 0

  gct-ones-loop : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gct-ones-loop (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else gct-ones-loop xs (i + 1) n (acc + list-at xs i)

  gct-score-all : List GaChromosome, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  gct-score-all (pop) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else gct-score-all pop (i + 1) n (list-push acc (gct-ones (list-at pop i)))

 The starting population is built here rather than by ga-random-population,
 and that is not a style choice.

 ga-rand-range is |seed * 2654435761 XOR idx * 40503| mod range. Both
 multipliers are odd, so for range 2 the answer reduces to
 lowbit(seed) XOR lowbit(idx): gene i of every chromosome is f(seed) with the
 parity of i flipped in, an alternating pattern, and therefore exactly half
 ones in every chromosome whatever the seed. Measured: a 30-individual,
 24-gene population from ga-random-population scored 12 for all thirty.

 That is a real defect in the helper and it is recorded in the changelist
 rather than fixed here, because ga-rand-range is what ga-evolve's tournament
 and mutation both draw on and changing it moves their behaviour.

 Its consequence for a test is worse than the flat scores: with every score
 equal, a ranking assertion cannot fail, because an all-equal list is both
 ascending and descending. The fixture below gives thirty distinct-ish
 scores, so ranking has something to get wrong.

  gct-bits : Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  gct-bits (ones) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else gct-bits ones (i + 1) n (list-push acc (if i < ones then 1 else 0))

  gct-seed-pop : Integer, Integer, List GaChromosome -> List GaChromosome
  gct-seed-pop (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let ones = int-mod (i * 7) 19
    in gct-seed-pop (i + 1) n (list-push acc (GaChromosome { genes = gct-bits ones 0 gct-genes [], gene-count = gct-genes }))

Section: The operators the domain supplies

  gct-breed : GaChromosome, GaChromosome, Integer -> GaChromosome
  gct-breed (a) (b) (seed) = ga-crossover a b seed

  gct-mutate : GaChromosome, Integer -> GaChromosome
  gct-mutate (c) (seed) = ga-mutate c gct-cfg seed

  gct-mutate-off : GaChromosome, Integer -> GaChromosome
  gct-mutate-off (c) (seed) = ga-mutate c gct-cfg-nomut seed

Section: The run

 The mutate operator is a parameter, so the same driver runs both arms.

  gct-run : List GaChromosome, Integer, Integer, (GaChromosome, Integer -> GaChromosome), List Integer -> List Integer
  gct-run (pop) (gen) (seed) (mut) (acc) =
    if gen >= gct-gens then acc
    else let scores = gct-score-all pop 0 gct-pop-size []
    in let best = gct-max scores 0 (list-length scores) 0
    in let next = ga-elitist-step pop scores gct-elite gct-breed mut (seed + gen * 13)
    in gct-run next (gen + 1) seed mut (list-push acc best)

 The recorded statistic is the population TOTAL, not its maximum. The maximum
 is too blunt to see this: the fixture's chromosomes are prefixes (m ones then
 zeros), a single-point crossover of two prefixes is another prefix, and its
 one-count never exceeds the better parent, so the best sits at 18 whether
 every child is a clone or every child is a crossover. The total moves,
 because it describes the whole generation rather than its luckiest member.

  gct-sum : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gct-sum (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else gct-sum xs (i + 1) n (acc + list-at xs i)

  gct-tourney : GaPopulation, GaConfig, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  gct-tourney (pop) (cfg) (gen) (n) (seed) (acc) =
    if gen >= n then acc
    else let scores = gct-score-all (pop.individuals) 0 gct-pop-size []
    in let scored = ga-set-fitness pop scores
    in let total = gct-sum scores 0 (list-length scores) 0
    in let next = ga-evolve scored cfg (seed + gen * 13)
    in gct-tourney next cfg (gen + 1) n seed (list-push acc total)

  gct-same : List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  gct-same (a) (b) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then True
    else if list-at a i /= list-at b i then False
    else gct-same a b (i + 1) n

  gct-max : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gct-max (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let v = list-at xs i
    in gct-max xs (i + 1) n (if v > acc then v else acc)

Section: Checks

  gct-monotonic : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  gct-monotonic (xs) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then True
    else if list-at xs i < list-at xs (i - 1) then False
    else gct-monotonic xs (i + 1) n

  gct-descending : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  gct-descending (xs) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then True
    else if list-at xs i > list-at xs (i - 1) then False
    else gct-descending xs (i + 1) n

  gct-first-at : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gct-first-at (xs) (target) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then 0 - 1
    else if list-at xs i >= target then i
    else gct-first-at xs target (i + 1) n

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let inds = gct-seed-pop 0 gct-pop-size []
    in let raw = gct-score-all inds 0 gct-pop-size []
    in let ranked = ga-rank inds raw
    in let ranked-scores = gct-score-all ranked 0 gct-pop-size []
    in let bests = gct-run inds 0 20260725 gct-mutate []
    in let flat = gct-run inds 0 20260725 gct-mutate-off []
    in let n = list-length bests
    in let first = list-at bests 0
    in let final = list-at bests (n - 1)
    in let final-nm = list-at flat (n - 1)
    in let hit = gct-first-at bests gct-genes 0 n
    in let solved = final == gct-genes
    in let solved-nm = final-nm == gct-genes
    in let gp = GaPopulation { individuals = inds, fitness = raw, pop-size = gct-pop-size, gene-count = gct-genes, generation = 0 }
    in let t-nox = gct-tourney gp gct-cfg-nox 0 8 777 []
    in let t-allx = gct-tourney gp gct-cfg-allx 0 8 777 []
    in act
      print-line-uni ("raw head:       " & gct-fmt raw 0 8 "")
      print-line-uni ("ranked head:    " & gct-fmt ranked-scores 0 8 "")
      print-line-uni ("optimum:        " & show gct-genes)
      print-line-uni ("first best:     " & show first)
      print-line-uni ("final best:     " & show final)
      print-line-uni ("solved:         " & show solved)
      print-line-uni ("solved at gen:  " & show hit)
      print-line-uni ("improved by:    " & show (final - first))
      print-line-uni ("monotonic:      " & show (gct-monotonic bests 1 n))
      print-line-uni ("rank descends:  " & show (gct-descending ranked-scores 1 (list-length ranked-scores)))
      print-line-uni ("no-mutation:    " & show final-nm)
      print-line-uni ("mutation earns: " & show (solved & (gct-not solved-nm)))
      print-line-uni ("generations:    " & show n)
      print-line-uni ("tourney x=0:    " & gct-fmt t-nox 0 (list-length t-nox) "")
      print-line-uni ("tourney x=1000: " & gct-fmt t-allx 0 (list-length t-allx) "")
      print-line-uni ("crossover live: " & show (gct-not (gct-same t-nox t-allx 0 (list-length t-nox))))
    end

  gct-not : Boolean -> Boolean
  gct-not (b) = if b then False else True

  gct-fmt : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  gct-fmt (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let sep = if i == 0 then "" else " "
    in gct-fmt xs (i + 1) n (acc & sep & show (list-at xs i))
